Author: Hanjun Yoo
Subject: [PATCH] abstract_exp_config: None-guard camera_quaternion in freeze_task_config

A camera without an explicit quaternion (e.g. RandomizedExocentric or a
MjcfCamera that never had one assigned) leaves `cam.camera_quaternion` as
None. `list(None)` raises `TypeError: 'NoneType' is not iterable`, so
freezing an episode with such a camera crashes instead of persisting a
valid SavedEpisode. Read the attribute once and pass the literal None
through when it isn't set; otherwise keep the previous coerce-to-list
behaviour.

Upstream: https://github.com/allenai/molmospaces (pending PR)

---
 molmo_spaces/configs/abstract_exp_config.py | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/molmo_spaces/configs/abstract_exp_config.py b/molmo_spaces/configs/abstract_exp_config.py
--- a/molmo_spaces/configs/abstract_exp_config.py
+++ b/molmo_spaces/configs/abstract_exp_config.py
@@ -171,12 +171,13 @@ class MlSpacesExpConfig(Config, ABC):
             # Read the camera's positions and convert them to fixed cameras
             if isinstance(camera, MjcfCameraConfig | RobotMountedCameraConfig):
                 cam = task.env.camera_manager.registry[camera.name]
+                quat = cam.camera_quaternion
                 new_camera = RobotMountedCameraConfig(
                     name=cam.name,
                     reference_body_names=list(cam.reference_body_names),
                     camera_offset=list(cam.camera_offset),
                     lookat_offset=list(cam.lookat_offset),
-                    camera_quaternion=list(cam.camera_quaternion),
+                    camera_quaternion=list(quat) if quat is not None else None,
                     fov=cam.fov,
                 )
                 sc.camera_config.cameras[i] = new_camera
